<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="ch-gpio-interrupts">
    <title>GPIO Interrupts</title>
    <introduction>
        <p>
            Day 8 used an interrupt whose source was a timer.  This chapter
            extends the same machinery to a source you can press: a GPIO pin,
            routed through the EXTI controller, so a button generates an
            interrupt instead of being polled.
        </p>
        <objectives>
            <ul>
                <li>Configure an external (GPIO) interrupt from a pushbutton
                    through the EXTI controller.</li>
                <li>Write an ISR that shares state with the main loop
                    safely.</li>
            </ul>
        </objectives>
    </introduction>

    <!-- ============================================================ -->
    <!-- ROUGH: everything below is Day 9 material that has NOT yet    -->
    <!-- been authored through the chapter process (CHAPTER_PROCESS.md).-->
    <!-- Assume nothing is correct until checked against Day 9 ground  -->
